@title Controller panel: a virtual radio drives the receiver of a two-speed hoist (1920)
@area Live
@sizes 1920x1080
# Lane C2. Shift+L, then "Controller..." on the Live potentials card opens the Controller panel on
# the right (Simulate > Controller panel does the same). The fixture has one generic radio bound to
# the receiver -A1: E-stop chain and main contact in series ahead of the outputs, hoist outputs 1 to 4.
# The rocker springs back when the pointer lets go, so the hold uses mouse_down / mouse_up at the
# button's position for this window size (1920x1080: "up 2" is at 1654 232).
open qa/fixtures/radio-hoist.novo
wait 20
key shift+l
wait 20
click_text "Controller…"
wait 20
expect "Simulation of wiring and logic"
expect "Generic controller, not a specific product"
expect "Signals (1 of 15 high)"
expect "9 signals drive nothing"
shot panel-at-rest
check_layout
# Main latch on: the receiver's main contact closes, so the circuit is fed but nothing is selected.
click_text off
wait 10
expect "Signals (2 of 15 high)"
shot main-on
# Hoist up, step 2: the rocker closes both up outputs while it is held.
mouse_down 1654 232
wait 10
expect "Signals (4 of 15 high)"
shot hoist-up-2
check_layout
mouse_up 1654 232
wait 10
expect "Signals (2 of 15 high)"
# The motor page, with the rocker held again.
key PageDown
wait 10
mouse_down 1654 232
wait 10
shot motor-page-up-2
mouse_up 1654 232
wait 10
# E-stop: the chain contact opens and every output drops, whatever the rocker does.
click_text E-stop
wait 10
expect "E-stop pressed"
expect "Signals (0 of 15 high)"
shot e-stop
check_layout
